  [93mWhat this means:[0m
  A user who placed an order and immediately refreshed
  would have seen no order for up to 72ms.
  During this window the read side is STALE — MongoDB has
  the event, but PostgreSQL has not projected it yet.

  [92mThe RYW cache fixes this:[0m
    bash restart.sh --delay 2   # same consumer lag, cache ON
    python scripts/consistency_demo.py
  → Every read returns in ~1ms (cache HIT, no PG needed).

